-d '{'model': 'gpt-4o', 'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are a fair judge assistant assigned to deliver insightful feedback that compares individual performances, highlighting how each stands relative to others within the same cohort.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of two responses strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, choose a better response between Response A and Response B. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: "(write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (A or B)"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###Instruction:\n\nImagine you are a medical professional tasked with evaluating simulated doctor-patient conversations generated from summary notes. \nThese conversations should accurately reconstruct interactions based on the SOAP (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan) format provided in the notes.\n\nHere is the medical note:\n#############################\nCHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nJoint pain.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nThe patient is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease who presents with some joint pain.\n\nThe patient reports that her left elbow has really been bothering her. She states that she sits at her desk all day for work with her elbows bent. She reports that after work it is really hard for her to flex and extend her left elbow. She reports that it has been really stiff and painful. She also notes that she has noticed swelling on the olecranon of her elbow. She reports that she is right-handed, therefore, she can still write, which is great, but typing is difficult. She denies any numbness or tingling in her hands. She reports that she has some weakness in her arm but nothing too significant. She denies any fever or chills.\n\nRegarding her epilepsy, she reports that she has not had any recent seizures. She reports that her last seizure was a year ago. She reports that she is still taking Keppra.\n\nRegarding her depression, she reports that she started therapy last year and she is trying to avoid medications for this problem. She reports that therapy has been helpful, but she still feels down and stressed. She denies suicidal and homicidal ideations.\n\nRegarding her peptic ulcer, she reports that she was dealing with a lot of stress last year. She then underwent an endoscopy which showed that she had an episode of gastritis. She was subsequently diagnosed with peptic ulcer disease and started Protonix. She reports that she has not had any issues with her ulcer since the procedure and everything has been good.\n\nThe patient denies chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting. She reports that she does have a little bit of medial nasal congestion from allergies.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\n• Ears, Nose, Mouth and Throat: Endorses medial nasal congestion from allergies.\n• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain or dyspnea on exertion.\n• Respiratory: Denies shortness of breath.\n• Musculoskeletal: Endorses left elbow joint pain, swelling, and weakness.\n• Psychiatric: Endorses depression.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\n• Musculoskeletal: Examination of the left elbow reveals erythema and edema. Pain to palpation of the left olecranon. Warm to palpation. Pain with flexion and extension. Palpable left radial pulse.\n\nRESULTS\n\nLeft arm x-ray does not reveal any evidence of elbow fracture.\n\nEGD revealed an episode of gastritis.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nAnna Morris is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease who presents with some joint pain.\n\nPLAN\n\nLeft elbow pain.\n• Medical Reasoning: I believe she has left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma.\n• Medical Treatment: Initiate meloxicam 15 mg once daily.\n• Patient Education and Counseling: I encouraged the patient to use a pillow to rest her arm on. She may also ice the area.\n\nEpilepsy.\n• Medical Reasoning: She has been doing well on Keppra and denies any recent seizures.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue Keppra 500 mg twice a day. This was refilled today.\n\nDepression.\n• Medical Reasoning: She reports doing well with therapy.\n• Medical Treatment: Initiate Lexapro 10 mg once daily.\n\nPeptic ulcer disease.\n• Medical Reasoning: Her recent endoscopy revealed gastritis\n• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg once daily before meals.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] Hi Anna, how are you doing today?\n\n[patient] Hi, Doctor. I\'m okay, but my left elbow has been really bothering me.\n\n[doctor] I see. Can you tell me more about the pain in your elbow?\n\n[patient] Sure. I sit at my desk all day for work with my elbows bent. After work, it\'s really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow. It feels really stiff and painful.\n\n[doctor] Hmm, that sounds uncomfortable. Have you noticed any swelling in the area?\n\n[patient] Yes, there\'s some swelling on the back of my elbow, around the olecranon.\n\n[doctor] Alright. Are you experiencing any numbness or tingling in your hands?\n\n[patient] No, no numbness or tingling.\n\n[doctor] How about weakness in your arm?\n\n[patient] I do have some weakness, but it\'s not too significant.\n\n[doctor] Okay. Any fever or chills?\n\n[patient] No, none of those.\n\n[doctor] Alright. How about your epilepsy? Any recent seizures?\n\n[patient] No, I haven\'t had any recent seizures. My last one was a year ago.\n\n[doctor] Good to hear. Are you still taking Keppra?\n\n[patient] Yes, I am.\n\n[doctor] And how about your depression? How have you been feeling?\n\n[patient] I\'ve been doing okay with therapy. It\'s been helpful, but I still feel down and stressed sometimes.\n\n[doctor] That\'s understandable. Any thoughts of harming yourself or others?\n\n[patient] No, nothing like that.\n\n[doctor] Good. And your peptic ulcer, how has that been?\n\n[patient] I had a lot of stress last year, but an endoscopy showed I had gastritis. I was diagnosed with peptic ulcer disease and started taking Protonix. Everything has been fine since then.\n\n[doctor] That\'s good to hear. Any chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting?\n\n[patient] No, none of those.\n\n[doctor] You mentioned some medial nasal congestion from allergies, correct?\n\n[patient] Yes, that\'s right.\n\n[doctor] Alright, let\'s move on to the physical exam. I\'ll take a look at your left elbow. Can you show me where it hurts the most?\n\n[patient] It\'s right here, on the back of my elbow.\n\n[doctor] I see some erythema and edema here. Does it hurt when I press on this area?\n\n[patient] Yes, it does.\n\n[doctor] It\'s warm to the touch as well. How about when you try to flex and extend your elbow?\n\n[patient] Yes, it hurts when I try to do that.\n\n[doctor] I can feel your radial pulse here. Let\'s review your recent test results. Your left arm x-ray does not reveal any evidence of fracture. Your EGD showed an episode of gastritis.\n\n[patient] Okay.\n\n[doctor] Based on your symptoms and exam, I believe you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma. I\'ll prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once daily for this.\n\n[patient] Alright.\n\n[doctor] I also recommend using a pillow to rest your arm on and icing the area to reduce swelling.\n\n[patient] Got it.\n\n[doctor] For your epilepsy, continue taking Keppra 500 mg twice a day. I\'ll refill your prescription today.\n\n[patient] Thank you.\n\n[doctor] And for your depression, I\'ll start you on Lexapro 10 mg once daily. How does that sound?\n\n[patient] That sounds good.\n\n[doctor] For your peptic ulcer, continue taking Protonix 40 mg once daily before meals.\n\n[patient] Okay.\n\n[doctor] Do you have any questions or concerns?\n\n[patient] No, I think that covers everything.\n\n[doctor] Great. We\'ll follow up in 2 weeks to see how you\'re doing with the new medication for your elbow.\n\n[patient] Sounds good. Thank you, Doctor.\n\n[doctor] You\'re welcome. Take care, Anna. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ \nDoctor: Hi, I\'m Dr. Smith. What brings you here today?\n\nPatient: Hi, I have joint pain in my left elbow.\n\nDoctor: I see. Can you tell me more about your joint pain?\n\nPatient: Yes, it\'s been bothering me for a while now. I sit at my desk all day for work with my elbows bent and it\'s really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow after work. It\'s really stiff and painful.\n\nDoctor: Hmm, I understand. Have you noticed any swelling on your left elbow?\n\nPatient: Yes, I have noticed swelling on the olecranon of my elbow.\n\nDoctor: Okay. Are you right-handed?\n\nPatient: Yes, I am.\n\nDoctor: That\'s good. Can you still write with your right hand?\n\nPatient: Yes, I can still write, which is great, but typing is difficult.\n\nDoctor: I see. Have you experienced any numbness or tingling in your hands?\n\nPatient: No, I haven\'t.\n\nDoctor: Okay. How about weakness in your arm?\n\nPatient: I have some weakness in my arm, but nothing too significant.\n\nDoctor: I see. Have you had any fever or chills?\n\nPatient: No, I haven\'t.\n\nDoctor: Okay. Can you tell me about your past medical history?\n\nPatient: I have epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease.\n\nDoctor: I see. Have you had any recent seizures?\n\nPatient: No, I haven\'t had any recent seizures. My last seizure was a year ago.\n\nDoctor: Okay. Are you taking any medication for your epilepsy?\n\nPatient: Yes, I\'m still taking Keppra.\n\nDoctor: I see. And how about your depression?\n\nPatient: I started therapy last year and I\'m trying to avoid medications for this problem. Therapy has been helpful, but I still feel down and stressed.\n\nDoctor: I see. Have you had any suicidal or homicidal ideations?\n\nPatient: No, I haven\'t.\n\nDoctor: Okay. Can you tell me about your peptic ulcer?\n\nPatient: I was dealing with a lot of stress last year and underwent an endoscopy which showed that I had an episode of gastritis. I was subsequently diagnosed with peptic ulcer disease and started Protonix. I haven\'t had any issues with my ulcer since the procedure and everything has been good.\n\nDoctor: I see. Have you had any chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting?\n\nPatient: No, I haven\'t had any of those symptoms.\n\nDoctor: Okay. How about medial nasal congestion from allergies?\n\nPatient: Yes, I have a little bit of medial nasal congestion from allergies.\n\nDoctor: Okay. I\'m going to examine your left elbow now. Can you tell me if you feel any pain when I touch it?\n\nPatient: Yes, it hurts when you touch it.\n\nDoctor: Okay. The examination of your left elbow reveals erythema and edema. There is pain to palpation of the left olecranon. It\'s warm to palpation and there is pain with flexion and extension. The palpable left radial pulse is present.\n\nDoctor: The x-ray of your left arm does not reveal any evidence of elbow fracture. The EGD revealed an episode of gastritis.\n\nDoctor: Based on your symptoms and examination, I believe you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma. I\'m going to start you on meloxicam 15 mg once daily. I encourage you to use a pillow to rest your arm on and ice the area.\n\nDoctor: I\'m also going to continue your Keppra 500 mg twice a day and start you on Lexapro 10 mg once daily for your depression.\n\nDoctor: And for your peptic ulcer, I\'m going to continue Protonix 40 mg once daily before meals.\n\nDoctor: Do you understand and agree with the recommended medical treatment plan?\n\n