ily: No, I haven\'t had to use it recently.\n\nDoctor: Okay, good. And I see that you\'ve been smoking and vaping, but you\'re trying to quit. How\'s that going?\n\nEmily: I\'ve been trying to reduce my use, and I think I\'ve made some progress.\n\nDoctor: That\'s great to hear. And I see that you have a nebulizer, but you haven\'t needed it recently. Is that correct?\n\nEmily: Yes, that\'s correct. I only use it for upper respiratory infections or when I was a child a few times.\n\nDoctor: Okay, good. And I see that your Asthma Control Test score is 21. That\'s great. And your spirometry test today was better than it was in 2019.\n\nEmily: Yes, I recall that it was smoky from wildfires during my last breathing test.\n\nDoctor: I see. Well, it looks like you\'re doing well. I\'ll refill your EpiPen and I\'ll give you some instructions for your follow-up.\n\nDoctor: For your moderate persistent asthma, I want you to start using Alvesco 2 puffs twice daily. Keep your Wixela in case Alvesco doesn\'t work well. Continue using your albuterol as needed. And come back in 4 months to repeat your ACT and spirometry testing.\n\nEmily: Okay, I understand.\n\nDoctor: And for your allergic rhinitis, continue taking Zyrtec 10 mg daily as needed. And for your anaphylactic reaction due to peanuts, continue your strict avoidance of peanuts.\n\nEmily: Okay, I will.\n\nDoctor: Great. If you have any questions or concerns, don\'t hesitate to ask.\n\nEmily: Okay, thank you.\n\n }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Reference Answer:\n[doctor] next patient is emily hernandez . date of birth , march 26 2001 . this is a 20 year old female being seen today for our yearly follow-up for asthma , allergic rhinitis and food allergy . due to insurance changes since our last office appointment in april 2020 , she was switched from symbicort to wixela . she also uses zyrtec in the spring , summer and fall for her seasonal allergy symptoms , which tend to work well . she also has known peanut allergy , she does toler