ackle football.\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] Hi Matthew, how are you doing today?\n\n[patient] Hi, Doctor. I\'m doing alright, but my shoulder\'s been giving me a lot of trouble.\n\n[doctor] I see. Can you tell me more about what happened?\n\n[patient] Sure. I was playing a game of pick-up football about four days ago. I got tackled a couple of times and landed hard on my right shoulder.\n\n[doctor] Ouch, that sounds painful. Did you return to the game after that?\n\n[patient] Yeah, I did, but the pain started after that. It\'s been pretty bad since then.\n\n[doctor] Hmm, where exactly is the pain located?\n\n[patient] It\'s on the back of my shoulder, just here.\n\n[doctor] Okay, and have you experienced any numbness or tingling in your fingers?\n\n[patient] No, no numbness or tingling. Just the pain.\n\n[doctor] How about the strength in your hand? Can you still grip things normally?\n\n[patient] The strength is okay, but I\'ve been avoiding lifting anything heavy because it hurts.\n\n[doctor] I understand. Can you touch your shoulder to your ear?\n\n[patient] No, I can\'t. It hurts too much.\n\n[doctor] Got it. Have you had any neck problems or other joint issues recently?\n\n[patient] No, no neck problems or other joint issues.\n\n[doctor] Any previous injuries to your right shoulder?\n\n[patient] No, this is the first time I\'ve had any problems with it.\n\n[doctor] Any fever or chills since the injury?\n\n[patient] No, but I did get a headache.\n\n[doctor] Did you hit your head when you fell?\n\n[patient] Yeah, I hit my head, but I didn\'t pass out.\n\n[doctor] Alright. Let\'s talk a bit about your medical history. Have you had any surgeries in the past?\n\n[patient] Yes, I had an appendectomy about three to four years ago.\n\n[doctor] Got it. Now, let\'s review some of your systems. Any fever or chills?\n\n[patient] No, none.\n\n[doctor] Any other joint pain besides your shoulder?\n\n[patient] No, just the shoulder.\n\n[doctor] How about headaches? You mentioned you had one.\n\n[patient] Yes, I\'ve had a headache since the injury.\n\n[doctor] Any numbness or tingling in your fingers?\n\n[patient] No, none.\n\n[doctor] Okay, let\'s take a look at your vitals. Your blood pressure is 122/76, heart rate is 82 beats per minute, and your oxygen saturation is 95% on room air. Everything looks good there.\n\n[patient] That\'s good to hear.\n\n[doctor] Let\'s move on to the physical exam. I\'ll start with your neck. Any tenderness here?\n\n[patient] No, no tenderness.\n\n[doctor] Full range of motion, good. Now, let\'s check your head. No trauma, no bruising or swelling. Now, let\'s examine your right shoulder. Does it hurt when I press here?\n\n[patient] Yes, that\'s painful.\n\n[doctor] Okay, pain on the posterior shoulder at the acromioclavicular joint. How about when you move your arm like this?\n\n[patient] Yes, that hurts too.\n\n[doctor] Decreased abduction and adduction to about 90 degrees, pain with supination and pronation. Your radial artery pulse is palpable. \n\n[patient] What does that mean?\n\n[doctor] It means that there is pain when you move your arm in certain directions, but your pulse is normal, which is good. We took an X-ray of your shoulder, and it shows an acute fracture of the acromioclavicular joint.\n\n[patient] Oh, that\'s not good.\n\n[doctor] It\'s not ideal, but we have a plan. I\'ll place you in a sling to support your shoulder. I\'ll also prescribe meloxicam 15 mg once a day to help with the pain.\n\n[patient] Okay, what else should I do?\n\n[doctor] We should get a CT scan of your right shoulder to get a better look at the extent of the fracture. I also recommend formal physical therapy to strengthen your shoulder. This will help in the long run and might avoid the need for surgery.\n\n[patient] That sounds like a lot.\n\n[doctor] I understand it can be overwhelming. It\'s important to avoid tackle football for now to let your shoulder heal.\n\n[patient] Alright, I can do that.\n\n[doctor] Do you have any questions about the plan?\n\n[patient] No, I think I understand. \n\n[doctor] Great. We\'ll get you set up with the sling and the medication. I\'ll also schedule the CT scan and physical therapy appointments. \n\n[patient] Thank you, Doctor.\n\n[doctor] You\'re welcome, Matthew. Take care and follow the instructions closely. \n\n[patient] Will do. Thanks again.\n\n[doctor] Take care, Matthew. See you soon.\n\n[patient] Bye. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ \nDoctor: Good morning, Mr. Allen. How are you feeling today?\n\nPatient: Good morning, doctor. I\'m feeling okay.\n\nDoctor: I understand that you came in today for an evaluation of a right shoulder injury. Can you tell me more about it?\n\nPatient: Yes, I was playing football a few days ago and I was tackled a couple of times and landed on my right shoulder. I had pain since then.\n\nDoctor: Hmm, I see. Where exactly do you feel the pain?\n\nPatient: The pain is located on the back of my shoulder.\n\nDoctor: Do you have any numbness or tingling in your fingers?\n\nPatient: No, I don\'t have any numbness or tingling.\n\nDoctor: Okay. And how is the strength in your hand?\n\nPatient: The strength is okay, but I have been trying to avoid lifting anything too heavy.\n\nDoctor: I see. Can you touch your shoulder to your ear?\n\nPatient: No, I can\'t because of the pain.\n\nDoctor: Okay. Have you been taking any medication for the pain?\n\nPatient: Yes, I\'ve been taking Tylenol, but it doesn\'t provide much relief.\n\nDoctor: I see. Do you have any neck problems or other joint problems?\n\nPatient: No, I don\'t have any neck problems or other joint problems.\n\nDoctor: Have you had any previous orthopedic injuries to your right shoulder?\n\nPatient: No, I haven\'t had any previous orthopedic injuries to my right shoulder.\n\nDoctor: Have you had any fever or chills since the injury?\n\nPatient: No, I haven\'t had any fever or chills, but I do have a headache.\n\nDoctor: